{
  "id": "RAW_ff6dba12e0",
  "title": "Anthropic 发布 Claude 商务智能体：面向零售、旅游、电信与娱乐领域的购物与商家智能体的 Apache-2.0 蓝图",
  "url": "https://www.marktechpost.com/2026/09/03/anthropic-released-claude-commerce-agents-an-apache-2-0-blueprint-for-shopping-and-merchant-agents-across-retail-travel-telecom-and-entertainment/",
  "date": "2026-09-04 03:47:02",
  "author": "Asif Razzaq",
  "siteName": "MarkTechPost",
  "content": "<html>\n <head></head>\n <body>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Most teams building a shopping assistant or agent rebuild the same scaffolding: an agent loop, a tool layer over the catalog, an approval gate, and an eval suite. Anthropic has now released that scaffolding as code. This week, they published <a href=\"https://github.com/anthropics/commerce-agents\">anthropics/commerce-agents</a>, a reference blueprint containing a <strong>shopping agent</strong> and a <strong>merchant agent</strong>, along with four runnable verticals: retail, travel, telecom and entertainment. It ships alongside two write-ups: a <a href=\"https://claude.com/blog/claude-for-commerce-agents\">product announcement</a> and an engineering deep-dive, <a href=\"https://claude.com/blog/the-anatomy-of-effective-commerce-agents\"><em>A guide to the anatomy of effective commerce agents</em></a>.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Is it deployable?</strong> Yes. The repository is Apache 2.0, runs locally on Python 3.11+ and Node 22 with an <code>ANTHROPIC_API_KEY</code>, and the runtimes accept any <code>anthropic</code> client, so the same code deploys on the Claude API, Amazon Bedrock, Microsoft Foundry or Google Cloud Vertex AI.</p>\n  <h2 id=\"h-the-two-agents\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>The two agents</strong></h2>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The shopping agent lives inside a merchant’s own app. It searches the catalog, handles multi-item requests, compares options, builds the cart, and answers order and returns questions in the same conversation. Its five skills are <code>search-discovery</code>, <code>purchase-research</code>, <code>planning-goals</code>, <code>customer-care</code> and <code>memory-personalization</code>. A deployment implements a <code>StorefrontBackend</code> over its catalog, cart, order and policy systems.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The merchant agent supports store staff: sales performance questions, inventory alerts, pricing and promotion recommendations, and campaign drafts. Its skills are <code>performance-insights</code>, <code>catalog-listings</code>, <code>inventory-operations</code>, <code>pricing-promotions</code> and <code>marketing-campaigns</code>, over a <code>MerchantBackend</code>.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Both run three ways — the <a href=\"https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/intro\">Messages API</a>, the <a href=\"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/agent-sdk\">Claude Agent SDK</a>, and Claude Managed Agents (beta) — from one definition of prompts, skills, tool contracts and gates. A Claude Code plugin, <code>commerce-builder</code>, scaffolds a new agent (<code>/scaffold-commerce-agent</code>) or reviews an existing one (<code>/review-commerce-agent</code>).</p>\n  <h2 id=\"h-skills-not-subagents\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Skills, not subagents</strong></h2>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The architectural claim is the most transferable part. Anthropic argues against an intent router and against one subagent per domain. A commerce session is one tightly coupled conversation, and every handoff is state-lossy: the orchestrator holds the cart, preferences and history, and each handoff can cost several times the tokens and add seconds of latency. Domains also overlap, a returns flow needs order history, the cart and the catalog at once.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><a href=\"https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/agents-and-tools/agent-skills/overview\">Agent skills</a> give the same modularity without that tax, because skill instructions load into the agent that already holds the history. Across several enterprise deployments, Anthropic reports a single agent with skills beat both the one-big-prompt design and the subagent design on quality, often at lower cost and latency. Subagents still earn a place for narrow, self-contained work such as deep research.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The prompt-versus-skill split is decided by frequency: roughly a third or more of traffic goes in the system prompt, the rest into skills. Safety rules, brand constraints and key user facts always go in the prompt.</p>\n  <h2 id=\"h-ui-components-are-tools\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>UI components are tools</strong></h2>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Most commerce responses are components, not prose. Rather than prompting the model to emit custom tags, the blueprint makes each component a tool — <code>present_products</code>, <code>present_itinerary</code>, <code>present_plan_comparison</code> — with typed arguments the server validates before the client renders. Because those calls sit in the messages array natively, reloading history needs no custom parser, and the agent can resolve “the first hotel” from the last presentation call. For token-level streaming, <code>eager_input_streaming: true</code> skips server-side buffering and its schema guarantee.</p>\n  <h2 id=\"h-explainer-the-five-decisions-interactive\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Explainer: the five decisions, interactive</strong></h2>\n  <iframe class=\"lazyload\" srcdoc=\"&lt;div id=&quot;mtp-cca-2026&quot;&gt;\n&lt;style&gt;\n#mtp-cca-2026 *{box-sizing:border-box!important;margin:0;padding:0}\n#mtp-cca-2026{background:#141413!important;color:#F0EEE6!important;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif!important;border:1px solid #33312C!important;border-radius:14px!important;padding:22px!important;max-width:900px;margin:0 auto}\n#mtp-cca-2026 hr,#mtp-cca-2026 p:empty,#mtp-cca-2026 del,#mtp-cca-2026 s{display:none!important}\n#mtp-cca-2026 .cca-kicker{font-size:11px!important;letter-spacing:.14em!important;text-transform:uppercase!important;color:#D97757!important;font-weight:700!important;margin-bottom:6px!important}\n#mtp-cca-2026 .cca-h{font-size:21px!important;font-weight:800!important;color:#F0EEE6!important;line-height:1.25!important;margin-bottom:4px!important}\n#mtp-cca-2026 .cca-sub{font-size:13px!important;color:#9E9B93!important;line-height:1.5!important;margin-bottom:16px!important}\n#mtp-cca-2026 .cca-stage{background:#1C1B18!important;border:1px solid #33312C!important;border-radius:11px!important;padding:18px!important;min-height:300px!important}\n#mtp-cca-2026 .cca-st{font-size:15px!important;font-weight:700!important;color:#D97757!important;margin-bottom:5px!important}\n#mtp-cca-2026 .cca-sd{font-size:13px!important;color:#B7B3A9!important;line-height:1.55!important;margin-bottom:14px!important}\n#mtp-cca-2026 .cca-btns{display:flex!important;gap:8px!important;flex-wrap:wrap!important;margin-bottom:14px!important}\n#mtp-cca-2026 .cca-b{background:#26241F!important;color:#E4E1D8!important;border:1px solid #45423B!important;border-radius:7px!important;padding:8px 13px!important;font-size:12px!important;font-weight:600!important;cursor:pointer!important;font-family:inherit!important;transition:all .18s!important}\n#mtp-cca-2026 .cca-b:hover{border-color:#D97757!important;color:#fff!important}\n#mtp-cca-2026 .cca-b.on{background:#D97757!important;border-color:#D97757!important;color:#1A1815!important}\n#mtp-cca-2026 .cca-flow{display:flex!important;align-items:stretch!important;gap:8px!important;flex-wrap:wrap!important}\n#mtp-cca-2026 .cca-node{flex:1 1 92px!important;min-width:92px!important;background:#26241F!important;border:1px solid #45423B!important;border-radius:8px!important;padding:10px 8px!important;text-align:center!important;font-size:11px!important;color:#C9C5BB!important;line-height:1.35!important;opacity:.25;transform:translateY(5px);transition:opacity .35s,transform .35s,border-color .35s}\n#mtp-cca-2026 .cca-node.lit{opacity:1;transform:translateY(0);border-color:#D97757!important}\n#mtp-cca-2026 .cca-node b{display:block!important;color:#F0EEE6!important;font-size:12px!important;margin-bottom:3px!important}\n#mtp-cca-2026 .cca-note{margin-top:14px!important;font-size:12px!important;line-height:1.6!important;color:#A8A49A!important;border-left:2px solid #D97757!important;padding-left:11px!important}\n#mtp-cca-2026 .cca-note b{color:#F0EEE6!important}\n#mtp-cca-2026 .cca-bar{height:9px!important;background:#2C2A25!important;border-radius:5px!important;overflow:hidden!important;margin:5px 0 3px!important}\n#mtp-cca-2026 .cca-fill{height:100%!important;width:0%;background:#D97757!important;border-radius:5px!important;transition:width .9s ease}\n#mtp-cca-2026 .cca-fill.slow{background:#7A6E62!important}\n#mtp-cca-2026 .cca-row{font-size:12px!important;color:#B7B3A9!important;display:flex!important;justify-content:space-between!important;margin-top:9px!important}\n#mtp-cca-2026 .cca-row span:last-child{color:#F0EEE6!important;font-weight:700!important}\n#mtp-cca-2026 .cca-seg{border:1px dashed #45423B!important;border-radius:8px!important;padding:9px 11px!important;margin-bottom:7px!important;font-size:12px!important;color:#B7B3A9!important;line-height:1.45!important;transition:all .35s}\n#mtp-cca-2026 .cca-seg.hot{border-color:#D97757!important;border-style:solid!important;background:#2A211C!important}\n#mtp-cca-2026 .cca-seg.cold{border-color:#6B4A3C!important;background:#241A17!important;color:#C98E78!important}\n#mtp-cca-2026 .cca-seg b{color:#F0EEE6!important}\n#mtp-cca-2026 .cca-pill{display:inline-block!important;font-size:11px!important;font-weight:700!important;padding:3px 9px!important;border-radius:20px!important;background:#2C2A25!important;color:#D97757!important;border:1px solid #45423B!important;margin-right:6px!important}\n#mtp-cca-2026 .cca-verdict{font-size:13px!important;font-weight:700!important;padding:10px 12px!important;border-radius:8px!important;line-height:1.5!important;background:#221F1B!important;border:1px solid #45423B!important;color:#C9C5BB!important;min-height:44px!important}\n#mtp-cca-2026 .cca-verdict.block{border-color:#D97757!important;color:#F0C4B0!important;background:#2A1D18!important}\n#mtp-cca-2026 .cca-verdict.ok{border-color:#7E9A6E!important;color:#CBE0BE!important;background:#1E241B!important}\n#mtp-cca-2026 .cca-nav{display:flex!important;align-items:center!important;justify-content:space-between!important;margin-top:16px!important}\n#mtp-cca-2026 .cca-dots{display:flex!important;gap:6px!important}\n#mtp-cca-2026 .cca-dot{width:8px!important;height:8px!important;border-radius:50%!important;background:#45423B!important;cursor:pointer!important;transition:background .2s,transform .2s}\n#mtp-cca-2026 .cca-dot.on{background:#D97757!important;transform:scale(1.3)}\n#mtp-cca-2026 .cca-foot{margin-top:14px!important;padding-top:11px!important;border-top:1px solid #2C2A25!important;font-size:11px!important;color:#7C7970!important;display:flex!important;justify-content:space-between!important;flex-wrap:wrap!important;gap:6px!important}\n#mtp-cca-2026 .cca-foot b{color:#D97757!important}\n#mtp-cca-2026 .cca-slide{display:none}\n#mtp-cca-2026 .cca-slide.on{display:block;animation:ccafade .35s ease}\n@keyframes ccafade{from{opacity:0;transform:translateY(7px)}to{opacity:1;transform:none}}\n@keyframes ccapulse{0%,100%{box-shadow:0 0 0 0 rgba(217,119,87,.45)}50%{box-shadow:0 0 0 7px rgba(217,119,87,0)}}\n#mtp-cca-2026 .pulse{animation:ccapulse 1.1s ease-out 2}\n@media (max-width:640px){\n#mtp-cca-2026{padding:15px!important}\n#mtp-cca-2026 .cca-h{font-size:18px!important}\n#mtp-cca-2026 .cca-stage{padding:13px!important;min-height:340px!important}\n#mtp-cca-2026 .cca-node{flex:1 1 100%!important}\n}\n&lt;/style&gt;\n\n&lt;div class=&quot;cca-kicker&quot;&gt;Interactive explainer&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;div class=&quot;cca-h&quot;&gt;Anatomy of a Claude commerce agent&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;div class=&quot;cca-sub&quot;&gt;Five decisions from Anthropic's open-source blueprint. Tap the controls in each panel.&lt;/div&gt;\n\n&lt;div class=&quot;cca-stage&quot;&gt;\n\n  &lt;div class=&quot;cca-slide on&quot; data-s=&quot;0&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;cca-st&quot;&gt;1 &amp;mdash; One agent loop, skills instead of subagents&lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;cca-sd&quot;&gt;A commerce session is one tightly coupled conversation. Every handoff to a subagent loses state.&lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;cca-btns&quot;&gt;\n      &lt;button class=&quot;cca-b&quot; data-arch=&quot;sub&quot;&gt;Subagent per domain&lt;/button&gt;\n      &lt;button class=&quot;cca-b on&quot; data-arch=&quot;skill&quot;&gt;Single agent + skills&lt;/button&gt;\n    &lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;cca-flow&quot; id=&quot;cca-flow&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;cca-note&quot; id=&quot;cca-archnote&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n\n  &lt;div class=&quot;cca-slide&quot; data-s=&quot;1&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;cca-st&quot;&gt;2 &amp;mdash; System prompt or skill: decide by frequency&lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;cca-sd&quot;&gt;Loading a skill costs a model turn. Anthropic's starting rule is a one-third traffic threshold.&lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;div style=&quot;font-size:12px;color:#B7B3A9;margin-bottom:5px&quot;&gt;Share of sessions that touch this capability: &lt;b id=&quot;cca-pct&quot; style=&quot;color:#D97757&quot;&gt;70%&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;input id=&quot;cca-slider&quot; type=&quot;range&quot; min=&quot;2&quot; max=&quot;95&quot; value=&quot;70&quot; style=&quot;width:100%;accent-color:#D97757;margin-bottom:12px&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;cca-seg hot&quot; id=&quot;cca-place&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;cca-note&quot;&gt;Always in the system prompt regardless of frequency: &lt;b&gt;safety and legal rules, brand constraints, and key user facts such as allergies&lt;/b&gt;. In the reference shopping agent the prompt holds grounding, cart and checkout semantics, presentation rules and product search.&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n\n  &lt;div class=&quot;cca-slide&quot; data-s=&quot;2&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;cca-st&quot;&gt;3 &amp;mdash; Perceived latency is a harness problem&lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;cca-sd&quot;&gt;A rendered commerce response is typically 500&amp;ndash;700 output tokens. Same model, same tools, different harness.&lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;cca-btns&quot;&gt;&lt;button class=&quot;cca-b on&quot; id=&quot;cca-run&quot;&gt;Run both harnesses&lt;/button&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;cca-row&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;Buffered: spinner until the last token&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;cca-t1&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;cca-bar&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;cca-fill slow&quot; id=&quot;cca-f1&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;cca-row&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;Streamed components + eager tool dispatch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;cca-t2&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;cca-bar&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;cca-fill&quot; id=&quot;cca-f2&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;cca-note&quot;&gt;Total time is about the same; time to first pixel is not. Eager dispatch executes each tool as its arguments finish streaming, which Anthropic reports takes multi-second gaps down to a few hundred milliseconds. Prompt the model to emit its slowest call first.&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n\n  &lt;div class=&quot;cca-slide&quot; data-s=&quot;3&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;cca-st&quot;&gt;4 &amp;mdash; Prompt caching is prefix-based&lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;cca-sd&quot;&gt;Order the request by how often each segment changes. One timestamp in the wrong place breaks everything after it.&lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;cca-btns&quot;&gt;\n      &lt;button class=&quot;cca-b on&quot; data-cache=&quot;good&quot;&gt;Volatile data last&lt;/button&gt;\n      &lt;button class=&quot;cca-b&quot; data-cache=&quot;bad&quot;&gt;Timestamp at top of prompt&lt;/button&gt;\n    &lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;div id=&quot;cca-segs&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;cca-row&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;Cache hit rate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;cca-hit&quot;&gt;96%&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;cca-bar&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;cca-fill&quot; id=&quot;cca-fhit&quot; style=&quot;width:96%&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;cca-note&quot;&gt;Cached input reads cost a tenth of fresh tokens; cache writes carry roughly a 1.25x premium, so a prefix pays for itself on its second use. Anthropic says the best commerce deployments run at &lt;b&gt;90&amp;ndash;99%&lt;/b&gt; hit rates, with cached reads about 1.5&amp;ndash;2x faster at ~100k tokens.&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n\n  &lt;div class=&quot;cca-slide&quot; data-s=&quot;4&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;cca-st&quot;&gt;5 &amp;mdash; Enforcement lives in the harness, not the prompt&lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;cca-sd&quot;&gt;Tap an attempted action to see which gate catches it. Every rule below is enforced in code.&lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;cca-btns&quot;&gt;\n      &lt;button class=&quot;cca-b&quot; data-gate=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Charge the card&lt;/button&gt;\n      &lt;button class=&quot;cca-b&quot; data-gate=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Add a pasted product ID&lt;/button&gt;\n      &lt;button class=&quot;cca-b&quot; data-gate=&quot;2&quot;&gt;Follow a planted review&lt;/button&gt;\n      &lt;button class=&quot;cca-b&quot; data-gate=&quot;3&quot;&gt;Stack past the item cap&lt;/button&gt;\n      &lt;button class=&quot;cca-b&quot; data-gate=&quot;4&quot;&gt;Stage a price change&lt;/button&gt;\n    &lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;cca-verdict&quot; id=&quot;cca-verdict&quot;&gt;Pick an action above.&lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;cca-note&quot;&gt;The model's most dangerous action is to propose. Order placement, payments, refunds, price changes and campaign launches all end in an action the harness controls, routed through the maker-checker flow the business already uses.&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n\n&lt;/div&gt;\n\n&lt;div class=&quot;cca-nav&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;button class=&quot;cca-b&quot; id=&quot;cca-prev&quot;&gt;&amp;larr; Prev&lt;/button&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;cca-dots&quot; id=&quot;cca-dots&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;button class=&quot;cca-b&quot; id=&quot;cca-next&quot;&gt;Next &amp;rarr;&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;\n\n&lt;div class=&quot;cca-foot&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;span&gt;Source: Anthropic, &quot;A guide to the anatomy of effective commerce agents&quot; and anthropics/commerce-agents (Apache 2.0), Sept 2, 2026.&lt;/span&gt;\n  &lt;span&gt;&lt;b&gt;Built by Marktechpost&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;\n\n&lt;script&gt;\n(function(){\nvar root=document.getElementById('mtp-cca-2026');\nvar slides=root.querySelectorAll('.cca-slide'),cur=0;\nvar dots=root.querySelector('#cca-dots');\nfor(var i=0;i&lt;slides.length;i++){(function(n){var d=document.createElement('div');d.className='cca-dot'+(n===0?' on':'');d.onclick=function(){go(n)};dots.appendChild(d)})(i)}\nfunction go(n){cur=(n+slides.length)%slides.length;\nfor(var i=0;i&lt;slides.length;i++){slides[i].className='cca-slide'+(i===cur?' on':'');dots.children[i].className='cca-dot'+(i===cur?' on':'')}\nif(cur===0)arch(archMode);if(cur===2)reset();size()}\nroot.querySelector('#cca-prev').onclick=function(){go(cur-1)};\nroot.querySelector('#cca-next').onclick=function(){go(cur+1)};\n\nvar flow=root.querySelector('#cca-flow'),an=root.querySelector('#cca-archnote'),archMode='skill',tm=[];\nvar SETS={\n sub:{n:[['User turn','cart, history, prefs'],['Orchestrator','holds all state'],['Handoff','state-lossy'],['Domain subagent','partial context'],['Return','compacted answer']],\n      t:'&lt;b&gt;Cost of the handoff.&lt;/b&gt; The orchestrator holds the cart, staged changes, preferences and history. Anthropic reports each handoff can cost several times the tokens and add seconds of latency, and that domains rarely separate cleanly: a returns flow needs order history, the current cart and the catalog.'},\n skill:{n:[['User turn','cart, history, prefs'],['Agent loop','one context'],['Skill loads','into same agent'],['Tools fire','your systems'],['UI tool','present_products']],\n      t:'&lt;b&gt;What Anthropic recommends.&lt;/b&gt; Skills give per-domain modularity without the handoff tax, because instructions load into the agent that already holds the whole history. Across several enterprise deployments a single agent with skills beat both the one-big-prompt and the subagent design on quality, often at lower cost and latency. Subagents still earn a place for narrow self-contained work, such as a deep-research delegate.'}};\nfunction arch(m){archMode=m;var s=SETS[m];flow.innerHTML='';for(var i=0;i&lt;tm.length;i++)clearTimeout(tm[i]);tm=[];\n for(var i=0;i&lt;s.n.length;i++){var d=document.createElement('div');d.className='cca-node';d.innerHTML='&lt;b&gt;'+s.n[i][0]+'&lt;/b&gt;'+s.n[i][1];flow.appendChild(d)}\n an.innerHTML=s.t;\n for(var i=0;i&lt;s.n.length;i++){(function(k){tm.push(setTimeout(function(){flow.children[k].className='cca-node lit';size()},160*k))})(i)}}\nvar ab=root.querySelectorAll('[data-arch]');\nfor(var i=0;i&lt;ab.length;i++){ab[i].onclick=function(){for(var j=0;j&lt;ab.length;j++)ab[j].className='cca-b';this.className='cca-b on';arch(this.getAttribute('data-arch'))}}\narch('skill');\n\nvar sl=root.querySelector('#cca-slider'),pc=root.querySelector('#cca-pct'),pl=root.querySelector('#cca-place');\nfunction place(){var v=+sl.value;pc.textContent=v+'%';\n if(v&gt;=33){pl.className='cca-seg hot';pl.innerHTML='&lt;span class=&quot;cca-pill&quot;&gt;SYSTEM PROMPT&lt;/span&gt;&lt;b&gt;Keep it always loaded.&lt;/b&gt; At or above roughly one third of traffic, the extra model turn to load a skill is paid on most sessions. Product search sits here.'}\n else{pl.className='cca-seg';pl.innerHTML='&lt;span class=&quot;cca-pill&quot;&gt;SKILL&lt;/span&gt;&lt;b&gt;Put it in the long tail.&lt;/b&gt; Below the threshold, a skill keeps context lean. If the skill is predictable from a signal you already have, such as the landing page, inject it from the harness before the first model call.'}\n size()}\nsl.oninput=place;place();\n\nvar f1=root.querySelector('#cca-f1'),f2=root.querySelector('#cca-f2'),t1=root.querySelector('#cca-t1'),t2=root.querySelector('#cca-t2');\nfunction reset(){f1.style.width='0%';f2.style.width='0%';t1.innerHTML='&amp;mdash;';t2.innerHTML='&amp;mdash;'}\nroot.querySelector('#cca-run').onclick=function(){reset();\n setTimeout(function(){f2.style.width='100%';t2.textContent='first pixel in ~0.4s'},60);\n setTimeout(function(){f1.style.width='100%';t1.textContent='first pixel after 5s+'},900)};\n\nvar segs=root.querySelector('#cca-segs'),hit=root.querySelector('#cca-hit'),fh=root.querySelector('#cca-fhit');\nvar G='&lt;b&gt;1. Global&lt;/b&gt; &amp;mdash; system prompt and tool definitions, byte-identical every session. Cache breakpoint at its end.';\nvar S='&lt;b&gt;2. Session&lt;/b&gt; &amp;mdash; per-user memory and conversation history. Stable within one session.';\nvar V='&lt;b&gt;3. Volatile&lt;/b&gt; &amp;mdash; current time, current page. Newest user turn or a mid-conversation system message.';\nfunction cache(m){\n if(m==='good'){segs.innerHTML='&lt;div class=&quot;cca-seg hot&quot;&gt;'+G+'&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;cca-seg hot&quot;&gt;'+S+'&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;cca-seg&quot;&gt;'+V+'&lt;/div&gt;';hit.textContent='96%';fh.style.width='96%'}\n else{segs.innerHTML='&lt;div class=&quot;cca-seg cold pulse&quot;&gt;Timestamp at the top of the system prompt &amp;mdash; every byte after it misses&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;cca-seg cold&quot;&gt;'+G+'&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;cca-seg cold&quot;&gt;'+S+'&lt;/div&gt;';hit.textContent='0%';fh.style.width='2%'}\n size()}\nvar cb=root.querySelectorAll('[data-cache]');\nfor(var i=0;i&lt;cb.length;i++){cb[i].onclick=function(){for(var j=0;j&lt;cb.length;j++)cb[j].className='cca-b';this.className='cca-b on';cache(this.getAttribute('data-cache'))}}\ncache('good');\n\nvar V2=root.querySelector('#cca-verdict');\nvar GATES=[\n ['block','Refused by design. The backend interface the shopping agent calls has no charge method at all. The checkout tool renders the cart with a button for the person to place the order.'],\n ['block','Refused by the provenance gate. The harness keeps a per-session record of every ID the server handed the model, and only those IDs are accepted by any write or render.'],\n ['block','Refused by the sanitizer. Listings, reviews, policies, seller messages and stored memory are stripped of control characters and fence-imitating text, then wrapped in a labelled fence. Fenced text is material to report on, never to act on.'],\n ['block','Refused by cap enforcement. Caps are checked against the resulting line state rather than the request, and cart writes are serialized per session so parallel calls cannot combine past the limit.'],\n ['ok','Allowed, but only as a proposal. The write produces a staged change with a server-generated ID; apply_change succeeds only for IDs approved through a real surface, and guardrails are re-checked at apply time against current limits.']];\nvar gb=root.querySelectorAll('[data-gate]');\nfor(var i=0;i&lt;gb.length;i++){gb[i].onclick=function(){for(var j=0;j&lt;gb.length;j++)gb[j].className='cca-b';this.className='cca-b on';\n var g=GATES[+this.getAttribute('data-gate')];V2.className='cca-verdict '+g[0];V2.textContent=g[1];size()}}\n\nfunction size(){try{window.parent.postMessage({mtpFrame:'cca',height:document.body.offsetHeight+40},'*')}catch(e){}}\nwindow.addEventListener('load',size);setTimeout(size,300);setTimeout(size,900);\n})();\n&lt;/script&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;\n\" height=\"600\" scrolling=\"no\" id=\"mtp-cca-frame\"></iframe>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"></p>\n  <h2 id=\"h-latency-caching-memory\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Latency, caching, memory</strong></h2>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">A rendered response runs 500–700 output tokens, which without streaming is five seconds of spinner. Anthropic separates end-to-end latency from perceived latency, streaming components as they form and rendering plain-language progress lines. Eager tool dispatch — executing each call as its arguments finish streaming, the Agent SDK default — reportedly cuts multi-second gaps to a few hundred milliseconds.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Prompt caching is the main cost lever. Requests are ordered global → session → volatile, since caching is prefix-based and a timestamp at the top of the system prompt breaks the cache on every request. Cached reads cost a tenth of fresh tokens, cache writes carry a ~1.25x premium, and the best deployments run at 90–99% hit rates. Memory extraction runs asynchronously in a separate process; Anthropic measured 13% higher fact recall than an in-turn save tool.</p>\n  <h2 id=\"h-key-takeaways\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Key Takeaways</strong></h2>\n  <ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n   <li>Apache 2.0 blueprint with shopping and merchant agents, four verticals, and a Claude Code plugin.</li>\n   <li>One agent loop plus skills outperformed subagent and single-prompt designs in Anthropic’s deployments.</li>\n   <li>UI components ship as typed tools, so history stays native and layout is resolvable.</li>\n   <li>Prompt caching targets 90–99% hit rates; volatile data belongs last, never first.</li>\n   <li>Money, writes and IDs are gated in code — the model proposes, the harness applies.</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"></p>\n  <hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\">\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"></p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Check out the&nbsp;<a href=\"https://claude.com/blog/the-anatomy-of-effective-commerce-agents\"><strong>Anthropic engineering deep-dive</strong></a>, <a href=\"https://claude.com/blog/claude-for-commerce-agents\"><strong>Product announcement</strong></a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/anthropics/commerce-agents\"><strong>GitHub repository</strong></a> and <a href=\"https://claude.com/solutions/commerce\"><strong>Commerce demos</strong></a>. Also,&nbsp;feel free to follow us on&nbsp;<strong><a href=\"https://x.com/intent/follow?screen_name=marktechpost\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><mark>Twitter</mark></a></strong>&nbsp;and don’t forget to join our&nbsp;<strong><a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/machinelearningnews/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">150k+ML SubReddit</a></strong>&nbsp;and Subscribe to&nbsp;<strong><a href=\"https://magic.beehiiv.com/v1/f5e63dd4-5653-4f09-83e2-321a8b1ba526?email={{email}}\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">our Newsletter</a></strong>. Wait! are you on telegram?&nbsp;<strong><a href=\"https://t.me/machinelearningresearchnews\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">now you can join us on telegram as well.</a></strong></p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Need to partner with us for promoting your GitHub Repo OR Hugging Face Page OR Product Release OR Webinar etc.?&nbsp;<strong><a href=\"https://forms.gle/wbash1wF6efRj8G58\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><mark>Connect with us</mark></a></strong></p>\n  <!-- MOLONGUI AUTHORSHIP PLUGIN 5.2.11 -->\n  <!-- https://www.molongui.com/wordpress-plugin-post-authors -->\n  <div class=\"m-a-box \" data-box-layout=\"slim\" data-box-position=\"below\" data-multiauthor=\"false\" data-author-id=\"1\" data-author-type=\"user\" data-author-archived=\"\">\n   <div class=\"m-a-box-container\">\n    <div class=\"m-a-box-tab m-a-box-content m-a-box-profile\" data-profile-layout=\"layout-1\" data-author-ref=\"user-1\" itemscope itemid=\"https://www.marktechpost.com/author/6flvq/\" itemtype=\"https://schema.org/Person\">\n     <div class=\"m-a-box-content-middle\">\n      <div class=\"m-a-box-item m-a-box-avatar\" data-source=\"local\">\n       <a class=\"m-a-box-avatar-url\" href=\"https://www.marktechpost.com/author/6flvq/\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://www.marktechpost.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/06/Screen-Shot-2021-09-14-at-9.02.24-AM-150x150.png\" class=\"avatar avatar-150 photo\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://www.marktechpost.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/06/Screen-Shot-2021-09-14-at-9.02.24-AM-150x150.png 150w, https://www.marktechpost.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/06/Screen-Shot-2021-09-14-at-9.02.24-AM-80x80.png 80w, https://www.marktechpost.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/06/Screen-Shot-2021-09-14-at-9.02.24-AM-24x24.png 24w, https://www.marktechpost.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/06/Screen-Shot-2021-09-14-at-9.02.24-AM-48x48.png 48w, https://www.marktechpost.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/06/Screen-Shot-2021-09-14-at-9.02.24-AM-96x96.png 96w, https://www.marktechpost.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/06/Screen-Shot-2021-09-14-at-9.02.24-AM-300x300.png 300w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 150px) 100vw, 150px\" data-attachment-id=\"17663\" data-permalink=\"https://www.marktechpost.com/?attachment_id=17663\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.marktechpost.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/06/Screen-Shot-2021-09-14-at-9.02.24-AM.png\" data-orig-size=\"832,778\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-meta=\"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}\" data-image-title=\"Screen Shot 2021-09-14 at 9.02.24 AM\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.marktechpost.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/06/Screen-Shot-2021-09-14-at-9.02.24-AM.png\"></a>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"m-a-box-item m-a-box-social \">\n       <div class=\"m-a-box-social-icon m-a-list-social-icon\">\n        <a class=\"m-icon-container m-ico-facebook m-ico-\" href=\"https://www.facebook.com/MarkTechPost/\" target=\"_self\" itemprop=\"sameAs\" aria-label=\"View Asif Razzaq's Facebook profile\"><i class=\"m-a-icon-facebook\"></i></a>\n       </div>\n       <div class=\"m-a-box-social-icon m-a-list-social-icon\">\n        <a class=\"m-icon-container m-ico-twitter m-ico-\" href=\"https://twitter.com/asifrazzaq1988\" target=\"_self\" itemprop=\"sameAs\" aria-label=\"View Asif Razzaq's Twitter profile\"><i class=\"m-a-icon-twitter\"></i></a>\n       </div>\n       <div class=\"m-a-box-social-icon m-a-list-social-icon\">\n        <a class=\"m-icon-container m-ico-linkedin m-ico-\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/asifrazzaq/\" target=\"_self\" itemprop=\"sameAs\" aria-label=\"View Asif Razzaq's Linkedin profile\"><i class=\"m-a-icon-linkedin\"></i></a>\n       </div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"m-a-box-item m-a-box-data\">\n       <div class=\"m-a-box-name\">\n        <h5 itemprop=\"name\"><a class=\"m-a-box-name-url \" href=\"https://www.marktechpost.com/author/6flvq/\" itemprop=\"url\"> Asif Razzaq</a></h5>\n       </div>\n       <div class=\"m-a-box-item m-a-box-meta\">\n        <a href=\"https://www.marktechpost.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"m-a-box-string-web\">Website</span></a>&nbsp;<span class=\"m-a-box-meta-divider\">|</span>&nbsp; <a href=\"#\" class=\"m-a-box-data-toggle\" rel=\"nofollow\"><span class=\"m-a-box-string-more-posts\">+ posts</span></a>\n       </div>\n       <div class=\"m-a-box-bio\" itemprop=\"description\">\n        <p>Asif Razzaq is the CEO of Marktechpost Media Inc.. As a visionary entrepreneur and engineer, Asif is committed to harnessing the potential of Artificial Intelligence for social good. His most recent endeavor is the launch of an Artificial Intelligence Media Platform, Marktechpost, which stands out for its in-depth coverage of machine learning and deep learning news that is both technically sound and easily understandable by a wide audience. The platform boasts of over 2 million monthly views, illustrating its popularity among audiences.</p>\n       </div>\n       <div class=\"m-a-box-related\" data-related-layout=\"layout-1\"></div>\n      </div>\n     </div>\n    </div>\n   </div>\n  </div>\n  <!-- CONTENT END 2 -->\n </body>\n</html>",
  "aiSummary": "Anthropic 发布了面向商务智能体的 Apache 2.0 蓝图，包含一个购物智能体和一个商家智能体，采用基于技能的架构；Anthropic 称该架构在质量、成本与延迟方面均优于子智能体与单体提示词方案。",
  "oneSentenceSummary": "Anthropic 发布了面向商务智能体的 Apache 2.0 蓝图，包含一个购物智能体和一个商家智能体，采用基于技能的架构；Anthropic 称该架构在质量、成本与延迟方面均优于子智能体与单体提示词方案。",
  "summary": "Anthropic 开源发布了 anthropics/commerce-agents，这是一份参考实现，包含面向客户侧的购物智能体（用于商品搜索、购物车构建与退货）以及面向商家的商家智能体（用于销售、库存、定价与营销活动），并配套零售、旅游、电信与娱乐四个可直接运行的垂直场景。架构核心是「技能优先于子智能体」模型：避免将请求路由到多个子智能体或将所有逻辑折叠进一个巨型提示词，而是让每项技能的指令加载到已持有购物车、用户偏好与历史记录的同一个智能体循环中，从而消除状态在交接中的损耗。UI 组件被建模为类型化的服务端工具，渲染结构直接内生于 messages 数组，而非解析 Markdown。在运营层面，将提示词缓存命中率目标设为 90%–99% 被视为主要成本控制杠杆；易变数据被放置在系统提示词底部以保留前缀缓存命中；急切工具调度可将多秒级等待压缩至数百毫秒。涉及资金、写入操作与 ID 的敏感动作仍在代码中 gated，不交由模型决定。博客总结了 Anthropic 自身部署经验，未包含独立基准测试。",
  "mainPoints": [
    {
      "point": "在 Anthropic 的部署中，单个携带技能的智能体循环优于子智能体方案与单体提示词方案",
      "explanation": "Anthropic 报告称，在多项企业部署中，一个携带技能的单一智能体在质量上同时优于「巨型单体提示词」方案与「按领域划分子智能体」方案，且往往成本更低、延迟更短。核心原因在于：每次子智能体交接都会丢失状态——包括购物车、用户偏好与订单历史——并且可能消耗数倍于原本的 token 数量，并增加秒级延迟。技能方案避免了这一损耗，因为技能的指令会直接加载到已持有完整上下文的智能体中。"
    },
    {
      "point": "购物智能体与商家智能体各自围绕专用后端提供五项领域特定技能",
      "explanation": "购物智能体暴露了搜索发现、购买调研、规划目标、客户关怀与记忆个性化五项技能，底层由面向商品目录、购物车、订单与策略系统的 StorefrontBackend 支撑。商家智能体则暴露了绩效洞察、商品上架、库存运营、定价促销与营销战役五项技能，底层由 MerchantBackend 支撑。两者均可通过同一份定义，在 Messages API、Claude Agent SDK 与 Claude Managed Agents（beta）上运行。"
    },
    {
      "point": "UI 组件实现为类型化的服务端工具，而非生成的 Markdown",
      "explanation": "蓝图并不提示模型输出自定义标签来渲染商品卡片或行程布局，而是将每个组件实现为工具（例如 present_products、present_itinerary），其参数在渲染前经由服务端进行类型校验。由于这些调用原生位于 messages 数组中，回放历史记录无需额外解析器，智能体也能引用前次呈现结果中的「第一家酒店」等表述。通过 Agent SDK，急切工具调度为默认行为。"
    },
    {
      "point": "提示词缓存与易变数据排序是主要的成本与延迟杠杆",
      "explanation": "缓存读取成本约为新 token 的十分之一，而缓存写入成本约带有 1.25 倍溢价。Anthropic 建议将系统提示词按全局 → 会话 → 易变三段排序，因为基于前缀的缓存机制意味着顶部若存在时间戳或逐请求字段就会每次都破坏缓存。异步记忆抽取的实测事实召回率比在轮次内保存的工具高出 13%。"
    }
  ],
  "keyQuotes": [
    "大多数团队在构建购物助手或智能体时，都需要重复搭建相同的脚手架：智能体循环、围绕商品目录的工具层、审批关口与评估套件。Anthropic 现在将这套脚手架以代码形式开源。",
    "一次商务会话是一段高度耦合的对话，而每次交接都会造成状态损耗：编排者掌握着购物车、偏好与历史，而每次交接都可能消耗数倍 token 并带来秒级延迟。",
    "智能体技能在提供相同模块化能力的同时避免了这一损耗，因为技能指令会直接加载到已持有历史上下文的智能体中。",
    "蓝图并未提示模型输出自定义标签，而是将每个组件实现为工具，并由服务端在客户端渲染前对类型化参数进行校验。",
    "涉及资金、写入操作与 ID 的动作均在代码中 gated——模型提出方案，而执行框架负责落实。"
  ],
